# The original parabolic and fixed-kernel counts in 14.7.73

The original natural and Steinberg coordinates give S=[S,L₁] and
P=[P,L₁](S∩P). Relative normality and the genuine Sylow witness identify
SP=O₂(L₁)=T∩K. The original qL maps O₂(L₁) to a four-group and T∩L to
an order-eight Sylow subgroup, proving |T∩L:T∩K|=2.

For an actual Sylow three-subgroup B of L₁, the same qL and qK coordinate
maps give |C_S(B)|=8 and |C_U(B)|=2. Coprime quotient lifting gives
|E/U|=4, and the natural P/E section gives |P|=2¹¹. The combined consumer
also returns the elementary P/U and its commutator generation.

All statements retain the original 14.7.71–72 inputs, original Steinberg
section, marked parabolic image and root geometry. Those inputs are
explicit obligations of their source producers and the parent 14.7.73
assembly. No desired core equality, index, fixed count, centralizer-product
identity or equality O₂(H)=P is assumed.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, printed pp.1076–1077, manuscript of 1 March 2004.
-/
